  "compatibility": [
    "WebGL2, ES modules and Pointer Events. A static architectural plate remains available without WebGL.",
    "Desktop mouse/trackpad scrolling, keyboard scrubbing and touch dragging. No automatic motion on arrival.",
    "Fixed GPU buffers, 28\u201372 coils and eight-sided wire. Rendering stops when progress is still; offscreen playback pauses.",
    "Tested in Chromium and Playwright WebKit. WebKit covers Safari\u2019s engine; physical Safari hardware may differ."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "One continuous helical wire follows a deformable centerline. The upper end anchors while the other turns over, lands, and becomes the next anchor.",
    "Every pose is calculated directly from normalized progress. Reversing, jumping, or pausing the timeline does not reset a physics solver.",
    "Curvature-aware spacing prevents the inner turns collapsing in an arch. Stair contact limits keep the wire above the treads.",
    "Eight consecutive descents by default, adjustable from six to ten. Four material studies, fixed or following cameras, and deliberate autoplay.",
    "An authored, physically informed movement study\u2014not a calibrated mass-and-spring simulation. Coils can extend; this is not a stress or engineering model."
  ],
  "reuse": [
    "Serve the exported ZIP over local HTTP and open example.html. Exact Three.js runtime is included; no build required.",
    "Use createSlinkyStairs from engine.js. Pass settings, optional tread geometry, and call setProgress with a normalized value.",
    "Use scroll-demo.html for a sticky editorial section driven by native document scrolling.",
    "Read README.md for the stair schema, integration, presets, lifecycle and motion limitations."
  ],
  "comparison": "none"
